  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advocacy, Communications and Capacity Building in Latin America for more equitable societies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports CAFOD&#x2019;s long term partner Comunicaciones Aliadas (COAL) in its strategic objectives of: 
- producing  information and analysis to inform public advocacy work, particularly in Peru and Andean countries, on social processes;
- strengthening  the communication skills for advocacy and campaigning work of social leaders, commentators and journalists in Peru and Andean countries;
- providing a communications advisory service and public advocacy accompaniment to social leaders, commentators and journalists in Peru.

It does this through:

(1)	Production and dissemination of information and analysis about key socioeconomic and human rights issues in Latin America and the Caribbean through weekly news alerts, its website, radio programmes and special reports;

(2)	Development of training materials, and running workshops, on communication and public advocacy for social leaders;  and the provision of advice for key social and indigenous organisations working on the defence of rights; 

(3)	Organising occasional events for journalists and social leaders to be informed about and debate key themes (roundtable discussions, press conferences, etc.), as well as two regional radio campaigns;

The project also includes capacity strengthening activities, so that COAL has efficient admin and finance systems, and a marketing plan for its news products.</narrative>
  </description>
